@title Your MRI Scan
@subtitle St. Anselm Imaging. What to expect, step by step.

!!! **Do you have a pacemaker, cochlear implant, aneurysm clip or any other metal implant?** Call the imaging desk on extension 2210 at least 2 weeks before your scan. Some devices need special planning, and your scan may need to be rescheduled.

## Before the day

- **Metal implants:** call extension 2210 at least 2 weeks ahead (see above).
- **Pregnancy or kidney disease:** tell us if you might be pregnant or have kidney disease.
- **Small spaces:** if they make you uncomfortable, ask your doctor about a mild sedative. If you take one, arrange for someone to drive you home.
- **Contrast dye:** if your scan uses contrast dye, do not eat for 4 hours before. You can drink water.

## On the day

1. Arrive 30 minutes early at the Imaging Department on level 2.
2. Bring a photo ID, your insurance details and your referral, if you were given a paper one.
3. Leave jewelry, watches, hearing aids and wallets in the locker.

! Wear clothes without metal zippers or underwire.

## During the scan

kpi Scan time | 30 to 60 min

- You lie on a padded bed that slides into a tube. The tube is open at both ends.
- The machine is loud. We give you earplugs or headphones.
- Keep very still. This helps us get clear pictures.
- You hold a squeeze ball. Squeeze it at any moment and the technologist will come.

## After the scan

- You can eat, drive and go back to work straight away, unless you took a sedative.
- If you had contrast dye, drink extra water.
- Your doctor receives your results within 3 business days.
- Your results appear in the patient portal after your doctor has seen them.

---

**Questions?** Call the imaging desk on extension 2210.
